---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../../assets/christian-dirnhofer.jpg';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { routePath } from '../../../i18n/routes';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  current="contact"
  title="Contact — Christian Dirnhofer"
  description="About Christian Dirnhofer and how to reach him."
  altHref={routePath('contact', 'de')}
>
  <div class="shell contact">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Christian Dirnhofer"
      width={180}
      height={180}
      class="portrait"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <p>Email is quickest. I usually reply very fast.</p>
    <ul class="links">
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">Email</span>
        <a href="mailto:christian@dirnhofer.net">christian@dirnhofer.net</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">LinkedIn</span>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/christian-dirnhofer-a89b4a229/">
          christian-dirnhofer
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">GitHub</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/Dirnei">Dirnei</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <section class="about">
      <h2>About me</h2>
      <p>
        Developer, at home in Bavaria. It started in 2007 with websites: HTML, CSS, PHP.
        Then VB.NET, then Java, and in 2010 C#. That one stuck.
      </p>
      <p>
        Embedded came along in 2012. Arduino first, ESP32 later, and I etched my own
        boards. I never quite got away from it. Then Minecraft plugins in 2013, and in
        between plenty of projects nobody needed. Building PCs ran alongside all of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        During the covid lockdown I built myself a CO2 laser. It still runs, so does the
        3D printer, and CAD is no obstacle.
      </p>
      <p>
        At some point the whole thing drifted towards DevOps, and in 2022 I stumbled
        into infrastructure as code and stayed there. At home there is Proxmox, Docker,
        Kubernetes, Ansible and Terraform. My home network is completely over the top
        because of it, and set up more cleanly than that of most companies I have
        worked for.
      </p>
      <p>
        If it can be automated, I automate it. In real life, and in games even more so.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block: 2rem 1rem;
  }
  .portrait {
    display: block;
    width: 180px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .contact p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .links li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
    padding-block: 0.75rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--red);
  }
  .about {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }
  .about h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 1rem;
  }
  .contact .about p {
    color: var(--text-body);
  }
</style>
